    {
      "id": "sec-003-executive-summary",
      "number": null,
      "title": "Executive summary",
      "level": 1,
      "pageStart": 9,
      "pageEnd": 11,
      "labelStart": "ix",
      "labelEnd": "1",
      "words": 717,
      "summary": {
        "text": "The executive summary describes the DQS as a flexible toolbox for assessing immunization monitoring systems at district and health unit levels, aimed at national and regional staff who adapt it. It aims to check the accuracy of reported immunization numbers and the quality of monitoring practices, in support of the Reaching Every District approach. Findings are analysed to identify strengths, weaknesses and practical recommendations, with the goal of building the most relevant options into routine practice.",
        "status": "draft"
      },
      "keywords": [
        {
          "term": "dqs",
          "heading": false
        },
        {
          "term": "district monitoring",
          "heading": false
        },
        {
          "term": "flexible toolbox",
          "heading": false
        },
        {
          "term": "immunization monitoring",
          "heading": false
        },
        {
          "term": "district levels",
          "heading": false
        },
        {
          "term": "improve district",
          "heading": false
        },
        {
          "term": "every district",
          "heading": false
        },
        {
          "term": "immunization activities",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "What is the DQS? The DQS is a flexible toolbox of methods to evaluate different aspects of the immunization monitoring system at district and health unit (HU) levels. Immunization “monitoring” refers to the regular ongoing measurement of the level of achievement in vaccination coverage and other immunization system indicators (e.g. safety, vaccine management). Monitoring is closely linked with reporting because it",
      "extractCut": true
    },
    {
      "id": "sec-004-a-introduction",
      "number": null,
      "title": "A. Introduction",
      "level": 1,
      "pageStart": 11,
      "pageEnd": 12,
      "labelStart": "1",
      "labelEnd": "2",
      "words": 59,
      "summary": {
        "text": "A footnote describing the Reaching Every District strategy and its five parts, from reaching the underserved to involving local communities in planning sessions.",
        "status": "draft"
      },
      "keywords": [
        {
          "term": "increasing",
          "heading": false
        },
        {
          "term": "immunization",
          "heading": false
        },
        {
          "term": "drop-out",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "1 Increasing immunization coverage at the health facility level. Geneva, WHO, 2002 (WHO/V&B/ 02.27). RED is a global strategy aimed at increasing coverage and decreasing drop-out rates. It is a five- part strategy: reaching the underserved, providing supportive supervision, increasing use of data for action, increasing micro-planning capacity at district levels and using local populations in planning immunization",
      "extractCut": true
    },
    {
      "id": "sec-005-b-immnization-data-quality-self-assessment-toolb",
      "number": null,
      "title": "B. Immnization data quality self-assessment toolbox",
      "level": 1,
      "pageStart": 12,
      "pageEnd": 37,
      "labelStart": "2",
      "labelEnd": "27",
      "words": 7242,
      "summary": {
        "text": "Presents the DQS toolbox options, summarised in a table of what can be assessed at district and health unit level. It explains in detail how to check reporting and recording accuracy by recounting immunizations across tally sheets, registers and reports and calculating accuracy ratios. Further sections cover completeness and timeliness of reporting, quality questions on the monitoring system, immunization card recording, vaccine wastage and safety monitoring. It ends with coverage denominators, which are explored through adaptable questions on quality.",
        "status": "draft"
      },
